			<div class="content" id="post-content-4385224">
									

<p>I think you could've hit the nail on the head even harder if you gave this article a picture to accompany it. A picture of what the individual looks like so that the humanization emphasizes the Foundation's inhumane efforts in order to uphold its own directives.</p>
<p>Even better if you gave this figure a name or described the anomaly as being a child or adolescent entity to further twist the proverbial knife in the audience that, no matter how old you are, the Foundation is willing to go that extra mile just to uphold its own values.</p>
<p>It just feels like with all of this, the article could finally flourish in its true potential, but in its current form, it offers little in the way of serviceable articles.</p>

