<p>Yeah, I think you're right; I added one and it looks better.</p>
<p>That said, I chose to not use a child/adolescent because I felt it'd parse badly considering they're meant to be doing a comedy show at a bar?</p>
<p>[EDIT: Okay so I was actually considering whether to make deeper changes so that'd work; cos e.g, they can run on stage mid-performance and narratively it'd work. That said, I think front-loading with it being a child would setup the horror too much: people would immediately suspect bad things and the whiplash from the discovery initially being almost slapstick in nature to it suddenly being dark feels like it would be less effective overall.</p>
<p>Plus I feel like it'd feel gratuitous? It wouldn't feel like there's a satisfying reason for it being a child other than because a child is more horror?]</p>

