<p>I respectfully disagree with this statement:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Even better if you gave this figure a name or described the anomaly as being a child or adolescent entity to further twist the proverbial knife in the audience that, no matter how old you are, the Foundation is willing to go that extra mile just to uphold its own values.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is already shown very well in this article from this statement:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The entrances to the venue were sealed with concrete blocks<sup>1</sup>; with an unknown number of police and patrons still inside.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This communicates that the Foundation not only sealed authorities, but <em>civilians</em> in an attempt to maintain secrecy and normalcy. There is a certain kind of horror of being trapped with a self-replicating person. There is another kind of horror in knowing that you can't get out, and there is only so much room and food left. Children need not be involved to be able to get that across.</p>

							</div>

								
					
