			<div class="content" id="post-content-4388136">
									

Hey cybersqyd,
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Here&nbsp;Be&nbsp;Crit&nbsp;/&nbsp;Opinion</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">ByeBye</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Nitpicks:</strong></p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-4518 instances are not immune to this and can cause the number of instances present to increase by counting themselves, even when only a single instance is present.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This sticks out sour to me, specifically &quot;SCP-4518 instances are not immune to this..&quot;, this makes it seem like the previous statement wasn't already referring to SCP-4518, could be solved by just removing that phrase, this also could just be a personal preference thing.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-4518 instances are visually identical, approximately 30 year old white males, with newly appearing instances being dressed in the same clothing as an existing instance nearby.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I feel like this sentence belong right after the first sentence of the description if not combined with that first sentence. Also wouldn't they all be wearing the exact same thing? If so the &quot; as an existing instance nearby.&quot; seems unnecessary.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>This was rapidly followed by many duplications as the audience saw what happened.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Instead of &quot;many&quot; maybe &quot;multiple&quot; would sound better.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The venue started to experience severe over-crowding, which lead to the venue owner phoning the police to clear out the venue.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Could just be me but &quot;phoning&quot; feels a tad nonclinical, maybe &quot;contact&quot; or something like it would work better.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>At this point, multiple SCP-4518 instances had spilled out onto the street.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Spilled out seems a tad nonclinical as well, &quot;relocated&quot; or something to that effect.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>..it was determined that the current supply levels for both sites was insufficient to handle the populations of SCP-4518 being contained there.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I think &quot;was&quot; should be &quot;were&quot;.</p>
<p><strong>Opinion:</strong> Okay little nitpicks aside I like this very much. In my opinion, it's a fantastic example of a simple idea done right. The subtle nod to MBMBaM is well done and doesn't try to overpower the article. While being a tad dark the overall situational humor of this really worked well for me. An easy +1.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
