																		Junior Staff - Site Criticism
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/tanhony" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(776854); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=776854&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606834635" alt="Tanhony" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=776854)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/tanhony" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(776854); return false;" >Tanhony</a></span> <span class="odate time_1570365611 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">06 Oct 2019 12:40</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4389865">
									

<p>Very nice! I realize this has already got some crit, but I just felt the need to go into why I dig this so much.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Tanhony&nbsp;rambles</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">TURN&nbsp;IT&nbsp;OFF</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>A few things I especially liked here:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>No monitoring of the interior of either of these facilities is to be carried out.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I’m a sucker for containment procedures that at first seem to go against the most basic forms of containment. It leaves me wondering why we can’t observe what’s going on here, which is of course the point, and just makes me want to know exactly what’s going on here even more.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>MTF Iota-10 requested a large number of transport vans to move the SCP-4518 instances back to Site 17.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>There’s a wonderful sense of dramatic irony here, with all the efforts Iota-10 are taking to manage the absurd numbers of 4518’s only creating more of them and making their job even harder. We can see that this is a serious situation, but it can’t help but be a little humorous as well.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The entrances to the venue were sealed with concrete blocks; with an unknown number of police and patrons still inside.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I feel like I got whiplash here in the best way possible. Suddenly, this isn’t funny <em>at all</em>. If this tone shift wasn’t taken care of properly, it could come across as jarring, but the way it’s done here just makes your stomach drop.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Incineration is to be done at a minimum temperature of 1500°C for at least four hours, with the ashes that remain being passed through a grinder to ensure none of the remains are identifiable.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The last line here, finally clarifying what the ‘biological matter’ that’s been referred to throughout the piece is, is a fantastic note to end on. It’s going to stick with me for a good while, I can say that much.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>A hearty +1!</p>
