<p>love those good good mcelroy boys! I had seen your opening note before reading (probably would not have caught the reference otherwise), so in my mind all of the comedians were Griffins, which only made the darker turn that much more tragic &#8212; I'm not sure the world could survive such a sustained loss of media luminaries even if virtually all of them <em>had</em> just been spontaneously generated</p>
<p>to the actual SCP: The timeline is well-paced and does a nice job of handling the hahaha-oh-wait-oh-no shift the narrative takes. I love the fridge-horror detail that it takes the Ethics Committee less than half an hour to terminate so much sentient life (and innocent bystanders), and that such a meeting and decision is so nonurgent as to receive hardly more emphasis than the details of the misinformation campaign.</p>
<p>Speaking of: my only nitpicks would be fairly minor grammatical/run-on sentence stuff. Like:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Following these events, a Foundation misinformation campaign was run to spread news of there having been a bar fight that got out of hand at the venue with property damage revealing the presence of asbestos, leading to the venue being sealed because of public health concerns relating to potential squatters.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is&#8230; just a lot of stacked clauses in a single sentence. Separating at that last comma instead with a &quot;&#8230; presence of asbestos. According to the campaign, this led to the venue&#8230;&quot; adds a bit more language but to my mind clarifies things tremendously.</p>
<p>Regardless &#8212; good stuff, you cool baby. +1</p>

